he race inside single digits, or sustained super PAC spending without an effective Suozzi response, could tighten this toward a tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tom Suozzi (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Tom Suozzi, a Democratic incumbent in an even partisan district, faces Republican Mike LiPetri in one of New York's most closely watched House races. Suozzi has built a large financial lead, with about $5.7 million on hand compared with roughly $700,000 for LiPetri, and has drawn backing from police and firefighter unions and business groups. Expert ratings lean Democratic, with most calling the race Likely D and a few Safe or Lean D, and prediction markets put Democratic odds near 88 to 90 percent.\n\nRepublicans are investing heavily: a Trump-linked super PAC has spent about $8 million on attack ads, and party groups are working to boost LiPetri. No public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals, ratings, and markets. Suozzi's incumbency and money give him a clear edge, but the sustained outside spending keeps the race competitive enough to watch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9133, "margin": 9.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.894, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8981, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.907, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8709, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8955, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9213, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9012, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8932, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8983, "margin